    "totalDuration": "1 yr 10 mos",
    "description": "My responsibilities include managing all Exchange Servers and Active Directory; I also head projects for upgrades to Network Infrastructure which included deploying new switchgear, correcting problems with VPN connectivity, and prioritizing IP traffic. In my position I was the technical leader in re-evaluating and revising our Amicas PACS system which was a 24x7 clinical application delivering services inside and outside of the hospital. I was also the lead technician in charge of upgrading, managing and maintaining our current EMC SAN solution, implementing a disaster recovery solution for PACS and Meditech, which is a clinical hospital information system. My responsibilities include helping to support, maintain and manage security for Amicas PACS system by supporting and implementing upgrades, CR, MR and Ultrasound Modalities, DICOM printers, upgrading and maintaining security for Exchange Servers, upgrading, developing, implementing and maintaining security for Microsoft SQL Server 7 and 2000, upgrading and monitoring Active Directory, modifying and improving Network Infrastructure and supporting Clinical Applications such as Meditech. I also manage, support and monitor our Dell/EMC SAN systems that hosts all critical applications for the Medical Center.",
